786
00:32:41,585 --> 00:32:43,336
I'll find someone
else to do it.

787
00:32:43,378 --> 00:32:45,088
I'd do it alone, but, uh...

788
00:32:45,130 --> 00:32:49,008
I don't know what happens
if the sea turtle catches you.

789
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:52,137
God, you know,
I feel so bad.

790
00:32:52,178 --> 00:32:54,306
I haven't seen you
this whole trip.

791
00:32:54,347 --> 00:32:55,682
Especially last night.

792
00:32:55,724 --> 00:32:57,183
Hey, don't worry about it.
It was fine.

793
00:32:57,225 --> 00:32:59,478
I ended up having the
best time with Rachel.

794
00:32:59,519 --> 00:33:00,978
I just felt bad for you,

795
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:02,397
stuck in that room
working on Ross's speech.

796
00:33:02,439 --> 00:33:05,525
Actually, it turned out
to be a lot of fun.

797
00:33:05,567 --> 00:33:06,860
Oh.

798
00:33:06,902 --> 00:33:09,863
Well, at least
we're both having fun.

799
00:33:11,657 --> 00:33:13,909
Is it weird that
it's not with each other?

800
00:33:13,951 --> 00:33:15,076
Yeah.

801
00:33:15,118 --> 00:33:17,621
A little bit, yeah.

802
00:33:21,583 --> 00:33:23,376
I think we need to talk.

803
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:27,965
Yeah, I think we do.

804
00:33:30,968 --> 00:33:32,970
About what?

805
00:33:35,054 --> 00:33:37,098
Come on, you guys,
it'll be fun.

806
00:33:37,140 --> 00:33:38,391
All right, all right,

807
00:33:38,433 --> 00:33:39,893
I'll play if we
don't keep score.

808
00:33:39,935 --> 00:33:42,354
Well, then how do we know
who wins?

809
00:33:42,395 --> 00:33:44,731
Nobody wins.

810
00:33:44,773 --> 00:33:46,733
So we're just four losers.

811
00:33:46,775 --> 00:33:47,776
Super!

812
00:33:47,818 --> 00:33:50,236
Well, I'm not
playing with her.

813
00:33:50,278 --> 00:33:51,446
I'm out.

814
00:33:51,488 --> 00:33:53,114
I'll play you.
Okay.

815
00:33:53,156 --> 00:33:55,408
Mike, you don't know
what you're doing.

816
00:33:55,450 --> 00:33:56,451
She gets crazy.

817
00:33:56,493 --> 00:33:59,621
This scar is from Pictionary.

818
00:34:00,956 --> 00:34:02,582
I think I'll be all right.

819
00:34:02,624 --> 00:34:04,459
You want to volley a bit
for serve?

820
00:34:04,501 --> 00:34:06,211
Sure if you want to.

821
00:34:10,590 --> 00:34:12,592
Oh!

822
00:34:12,634 --> 00:34:16,972
Oh, by the way, um, I'm awesome.

823
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:21,142
Oh, dear God,
there's two of them.

824
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:23,228
You ready to play?

825
00:34:23,269 --> 00:34:24,229
Hell, yeah.

826
00:34:24,270 --> 00:34:25,397
Did you know this
about him?

827
00:34:25,438 --> 00:34:26,481
No idea.

828
00:34:26,523 --> 00:34:29,484
I thought he was
soft like you.

829
00:34:29,526 --> 00:34:31,570
You want to make it
more interesting?

830
00:34:31,611 --> 00:34:32,946
How much were you thinking?

831
00:34:32,988 --> 00:34:34,239
Ten bucks a game.

832
00:34:34,280 --> 00:34:35,072
Make it 50.

833
00:34:35,114 --> 00:34:36,033
I'll make it a hundred.

834
00:34:36,074 --> 00:34:38,785
One thousand...
Okay!

835
00:34:38,827 --> 00:34:40,829
We'll flip to see
who goes first.

836
00:34:40,871 --> 00:34:42,330
You got a quarter?

837
00:34:42,372 --> 00:34:43,623
No.

838
00:34:43,665 --> 00:34:45,083
Either of you girls
got a quarter?

839
00:34:45,124 --> 00:34:49,671
Honey, try to focus
the trash talk on him.

840
00:34:50,923 --> 00:34:52,424
Monica, you call it.
Heads.

841
00:34:52,465 --> 00:34:54,133
No, tails! Heads!
Tails.

842
00:34:54,175 --> 00:34:56,887
Oh, what are the chances?!

843
00:35:00,348 --> 00:35:01,892
Ha! My point!

844
00:35:01,934 --> 00:35:03,351
Oh, no, I don't
think so.

845
00:35:03,393 --> 00:35:05,103
According to standard table
tennis rules,

846
00:35:05,144 --> 00:35:06,939
if at any time a player uses
his non-racquet-bearing hand

847
00:35:06,980 --> 00:35:10,943
to touch the playing surface,
he or she forfeits the point.

848
00:35:13,653 --> 00:35:16,448
He was a lawyer.

849
00:35:17,574 --> 00:35:20,410
All of the East Coast
is having beautiful weather.

850
00:35:20,452 --> 00:35:22,913
In New York it's 72 and sunny.

851
00:35:22,955 --> 00:35:25,331
Weather bitch.

852
00:35:25,373 --> 00:35:27,084
( knocking on door )

853
00:35:27,125 --> 00:35:28,627
It's open.

854
00:35:30,253 --> 00:35:31,421
Hi, Joe.
Hey.

855
00:35:31,463 --> 00:35:33,882
What, is everything okay?

856
00:35:33,924 --> 00:35:36,426
Charlie and I broke up.

857
00:35:36,468 --> 00:35:37,970
No. Why?

858
00:35:38,011 --> 00:35:41,514
Well, she said
we have nothing in common.

859
00:35:41,556 --> 00:35:43,058
That's crazy.

860
00:35:43,100 --> 00:35:46,352
No, it's not.
We have nothing in common.

861
00:35:46,394 --> 00:35:49,106
Yeah, that's true.

862
00:35:49,147 --> 00:35:52,609
I mean, she should be with
someone more like... Ross.

863
00:35:52,651 --> 00:35:56,071
You know, he uses
all those big words, too.

864
00:35:56,113 --> 00:35:58,907
Man, smart people are dull.

865
00:35:58,949 --> 00:36:00,158
Hey!

866
00:36:00,199 --> 00:36:02,494
( chuckles )
Okay, Rach.

867
00:36:03,996 --> 00:36:07,082
I feel so stupid, you know.

868
00:36:07,124 --> 00:36:09,584
Why do I keep going after
the wrong girls?

869
00:36:09,626 --> 00:36:11,920
Well, what are you
talking about?

870
00:36:11,962 --> 00:36:13,880
Come on, I mean,
there's you,

871
00:36:13,922 --> 00:36:15,548
then there's Charlie...

872
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:16,549
That's like...

873
00:36:16,591 --> 00:36:17,550
( sighs )

874
00:36:17,592 --> 00:36:19,594
What the hell's
my problem?

875
00:36:19,636 --> 00:36:21,805
( sighs )

876
00:36:24,516 --> 00:36:26,768
Okay. Um...

877
00:36:26,810 --> 00:36:29,771
maybe you're not always
going after the wrong girl.

878
00:36:29,813 --> 00:36:33,525
I'm telling you, Rach,
Charlie is not right for me.

879
00:36:33,566 --> 00:36:35,652
Yeah, I'm not talking about her.

880
00:36:35,694 --> 00:36:37,070
Well, then who?

881
00:36:37,112 --> 00:36:39,531
The waitress I went out with
last month?

882
00:36:39,572 --> 00:36:42,575
You know what?
Forget it.

883
00:36:42,617 --> 00:36:43,702
No, no, no, no,

884
00:36:43,743 --> 00:36:44,619
Who are you
talking about?

885
00:36:44,661 --> 00:36:45,954
I-I-I don't... I don't...

886
00:36:45,996 --> 00:36:48,999
I actually don't know
who I'm talking about.

887
00:36:49,041 --> 00:36:50,416
Okay.

888
00:36:50,458 --> 00:36:52,044
All right, well...

889
00:36:52,085 --> 00:36:53,962
I'm gonna go see if I can
get a room for tonight.

890
00:36:54,004 --> 00:36:55,964
And, uh,
I'll see you later.

891
00:36:56,006 --> 00:36:57,924
Yeah, sure. Okay.

892
00:37:23,491 --> 00:37:25,160
You like me?

893
00:37:25,202 --> 00:37:26,536
Okay...

894
00:37:26,578 --> 00:37:28,121
let's not make a big thing
about this.

895
00:37:28,163 --> 00:37:29,372
It's a huge thing.

896
00:37:29,414 --> 00:37:32,042
Okay, not working
with me, Joe.

897
00:37:32,084 --> 00:37:33,376
Look, here's
the thing.

898
00:37:33,418 --> 00:37:37,089
Lately, I have been
having thoughts.

899
00:37:38,297 --> 00:37:40,217
Musings, if you will.

900
00:37:40,258 --> 00:37:43,095
Wha... For how long?

901
00:37:43,136 --> 00:37:44,221
Only like a month.

902
00:37:44,261 --> 00:37:46,014
A month?!

903
00:37:46,056 --> 00:37:47,432
Dial it down.

904
00:37:47,473 --> 00:37:50,351
Listen, okay, and maybe
they're crazy thoughts,

905
00:37:50,393 --> 00:37:51,770
but sometimes I do.

906
00:37:51,811 --> 00:37:55,314
I've been thinking about,
you know, us.

907
00:37:57,234 --> 00:37:58,985
Okay, dial it up a little.

908
00:37:59,027 --> 00:38:01,988
Okay... I just have
one question.
Shoot.

909
00:38:02,030 --> 00:38:03,865
What the hell are you doing?!

910
00:38:03,907 --> 00:38:05,491
I'm not trying to do anything.

911
00:38:05,533 --> 00:38:07,619
It's just, we have such
a good time

912
00:38:07,660 --> 00:38:09,246
when we're together,
you know.

913
00:38:09,287 --> 00:38:11,873
Aren't you just
a little curious

914
00:38:11,915 --> 00:38:13,625
what it would be like?

915
00:38:13,666 --> 00:38:15,210
Am I curious?

916
00:38:15,252 --> 00:38:18,213
I'm as curious as... as...

917
00:38:18,255 --> 00:38:21,049
George.

918
00:38:21,841 --> 00:38:22,884
Who?

919
00:38:22,926 --> 00:38:24,469
Curious George.

920
00:38:24,510 --> 00:38:26,888
You know, the monkey
and the guy with the yellow hat?

921
00:38:26,930 --> 00:38:29,390
Yes, of course.
I remember him.

922
00:38:29,432 --> 00:38:30,767
He had a paper route.

923
00:38:30,809 --> 00:38:32,102
Yeah, he did.

924
00:38:32,144 --> 00:38:33,937
See, this is what
I'm talking about.

925
00:38:33,979 --> 00:38:35,354
Yeah, I know we're great,

926
00:38:35,396 --> 00:38:38,066
but, Rach, no, this...
this can't happen.

927
00:38:38,108 --> 00:38:42,821
Can't it just happen
a little bit?

928
00:38:42,862 --> 00:38:44,906
Well...

929
00:38:44,948 --> 00:38:47,575
No! No!
It can't happen at all!

930
00:38:47,617 --> 00:38:49,035
Why? Why not?

931
00:38:49,077 --> 00:38:51,328
Because, look, no one
wants this to happen

932
00:38:51,370 --> 00:38:52,789
more than me, okay?

933
00:38:52,831 --> 00:38:54,332
I have gone over this moment

934
00:38:54,373 --> 00:38:55,750
in my head a hundred times

935
00:38:55,792 --> 00:38:59,420
and not once did I ever
say no.

936
00:38:59,462 --> 00:39:01,256
But...

937
00:39:01,298 --> 00:39:03,258
( sighs )

938
00:39:03,300 --> 00:39:05,260
I couldn't do it to Ross.

939
00:39:05,302 --> 00:39:08,096
But that wasn't going
to stop you before.

940
00:39:08,138 --> 00:39:09,639
I know.

941
00:39:09,681 --> 00:39:12,642
I know, but I've thought
about it a lot since then,

942
00:39:12,684 --> 00:39:15,603
and it just wouldn't be right.

943
00:39:17,772 --> 00:39:19,983
I'm sorry.

944
00:39:22,235 --> 00:39:24,988
I'm sorry, too.

945
00:39:25,947 --> 00:39:26,948
Oh, God.

946
00:39:26,990 --> 00:39:28,366
I shouldn't have
said anything.

947
00:39:28,407 --> 00:39:29,284
No, no.
No, no, no.

948
00:39:29,326 --> 00:39:30,869
Hey, hey,
we'll be fine.

949
00:39:30,910 --> 00:39:32,954
Like you said,
it's no big deal.
It's not a big deal.

950
00:39:32,996 --> 00:39:35,081
No big deal.
It's so not a big deal.

951
00:39:35,123 --> 00:39:37,458
Yeah.
I'll see you later.
Okay.

952
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:39,002
Hey.

953
00:39:56,353 --> 00:39:58,271
( sighs )

954
00:39:58,313 --> 00:39:59,981
Oh!

955
00:40:13,411 --> 00:40:15,413
Oh! I'm sorry, I think...

956
00:40:15,454 --> 00:40:17,623
I think that may
have missed the table.

957
00:40:17,665 --> 00:40:18,917
Oh, do you?

958
00:40:18,958 --> 00:40:19,667
Uh, yeah.

959
00:40:19,709 --> 00:40:20,417
Do you? 

960
00:40:20,459 --> 00:40:21,169
Uh, yeah.

961
00:40:21,211 --> 00:40:21,920
Do ya?

962
00:40:21,961 --> 00:40:22,962
Uh, yeah.

963
00:40:23,004 --> 00:40:26,132
You really find this
attractive on him?

964
00:40:26,174 --> 00:40:27,424
Oh, yeah.

965
00:40:27,466 --> 00:40:28,634
Are you telling me
you're not even

966
00:40:28,676 --> 00:40:31,679
a little turned on
by Monica right now?

967
00:40:38,103 --> 00:40:39,687
I think this is the first time
in our marriage

968
00:40:39,729 --> 00:40:42,148
that I felt like
the more attractive one.

969
00:40:42,190 --> 00:40:43,691
PHOEBE:
All right,
come on, Mike.

970
00:40:43,733 --> 00:40:44,609
You can beat her.

971
00:40:44,650 --> 00:40:46,611
Knock that dog
off her head.

972
00:40:50,656 --> 00:40:51,366
Damn it!

973
00:40:51,408 --> 00:40:53,910
I sleep with him.

974
00:40:55,328 --> 00:40:56,662
Game point.

975
00:40:56,704 --> 00:40:57,705
Don't get too cocky.

976
00:40:57,747 --> 00:40:59,332
Remember, I won the last one.

977
00:40:59,374 --> 00:41:02,168
Oh, by the way, how did that
feel losing to a girl?

978
00:41:02,210 --> 00:41:04,254
You know, you should really
look in mirror

979
00:41:04,296 --> 00:41:06,381
before you call yourself that.

980
00:41:10,176 --> 00:41:11,552
No! No! No!

981
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:14,097
And that's how it's done.

982
00:41:14,139 --> 00:41:15,514
CHANDLER:
Okeydokey.

983
00:41:15,556 --> 00:41:17,058
You've each won a game

984
00:41:17,100 --> 00:41:19,685
and I've lost what's felt
like a year of my life.

985
00:41:19,727 --> 00:41:21,854
So everybody goes home a winner.

986
00:41:21,896 --> 00:41:22,814
Best out of three?

987
00:41:22,855 --> 00:41:23,815
That's what I'm thinking.

988
00:41:23,856 --> 00:41:25,442
Should I use my invisibility

989
00:41:25,482 --> 00:41:29,237
to fight crime or for evil?

990
00:41:29,737 --> 00:41:31,281
Serve the ball, chump.

991
00:41:31,323 --> 00:41:32,949
( imitating Monica ):
"Serve the ball, chump."

992
00:41:32,991 --> 00:41:37,036
Okay, better comebacks, Mike.
Better comebacks.

993
00:41:39,080 --> 00:41:41,958
I'm just saying I have
a cabin in the Adirondacks.

994
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:43,709
And if you ever want to get away
from the city,

995
00:41:43,751 --> 00:41:46,754
well, that'd be...

996
00:41:46,796 --> 00:41:48,547
just nifty.

997
00:41:50,758 --> 00:41:53,178
Ooh, well, um...

998
00:41:53,219 --> 00:41:55,888
I've kind of got a lot
on my plate right now.

999
00:41:55,930 --> 00:41:58,933
Not that I wouldn't love
a weekend in the country

1000
00:41:58,975 --> 00:42:00,810
with a strange man.

1001
00:42:02,479 --> 00:42:03,480
Jarvis?

1002
00:42:03,520 --> 00:42:04,897
Oh, you're back.

1003
00:42:04,939 --> 00:42:08,818
Um, this is my wife Nancy.

1004
00:42:08,860 --> 00:42:10,820
Get out.

1005
00:42:11,321 --> 00:42:13,781
Ross, can I talk
to you for a minute?

1006
00:42:13,823 --> 00:42:15,574
Yes, please.

1007
00:42:17,076 --> 00:42:20,621
Um, so what's
going on?

1008
00:42:20,663 --> 00:42:22,415
Um...

1009
00:42:22,457 --> 00:42:25,210
Well...

1010
00:42:25,251 --> 00:42:26,961
Joey and I broke up.

1011
00:42:27,003 --> 00:42:28,087
Oh, my God.

1012
00:42:28,129 --> 00:42:30,131
What... what happened?

1013
00:42:30,173 --> 00:42:31,757
Joey is a great guy,

1014
00:42:31,799 --> 00:42:35,345
but we're just...
we're so different.

1015
00:42:35,387 --> 00:42:36,804
I mean, like during your speech

1016
00:42:36,846 --> 00:42:38,639
he kept laughing
at Homo erectus.

1017
00:42:38,681 --> 00:42:40,433
I knew that was him.

1018
00:42:43,186 --> 00:42:45,355
Anyway, I just...

1019
00:42:45,397 --> 00:42:46,814
I think
it's for the best.

1020
00:42:46,856 --> 00:42:50,026
Hey. Hey, you okay?

1021
00:42:50,068 --> 00:42:51,986
I guess.

1022
00:42:54,489 --> 00:42:56,782
There was, um...

1023
00:42:56,824 --> 00:42:58,201
there was another reason

1024
00:42:58,243 --> 00:43:01,829
that I thought it was
time to end it with Joey.

1025
00:43:01,871 --> 00:43:07,419
I started to realize that
I was having feelings

1026
00:43:07,460 --> 00:43:09,837
for someone else.

1027
00:43:10,755 --> 00:43:12,882
Okay, Geller, last day
of the conference.

1028
00:43:12,924 --> 00:43:15,260
You know what happens
to the keynote speaker.

1029
00:43:15,301 --> 00:43:18,096
Uh, Professor Klarik,
we're kind of in the middle

1030
00:43:18,137 --> 00:43:19,638
of a conversation here.

1031
00:43:19,680 --> 00:43:21,349
Yeah. Can't you guys just
throw him in the pool later?

1032
00:43:21,391 --> 00:43:23,684
Or we could throw you both
in now.

1033
00:43:23,726 --> 00:43:24,936
Okay, gentlemen, please.

1034
00:43:24,977 --> 00:43:27,188
Aren't we a little
old for this?

1035
00:43:27,230 --> 00:43:28,356
I mean,

1036
00:43:28,398 --> 00:43:30,108
we're scientists,
all right?

1037
00:43:30,149 --> 00:43:31,025
We're academics,

1038
00:43:31,067 --> 00:43:32,277
and most importantly,

1039
00:43:32,318 --> 00:43:34,571
you will have
to catch us first.

1040
00:43:34,612 --> 00:43:36,364
Go! Go! Go!

1041
00:43:45,582 --> 00:43:49,127
Okay, so it's tied again:
41 to 41.

1042
00:43:50,587 --> 00:43:53,005
Okay, look, enough
is enough.

1043
00:43:53,047 --> 00:43:55,133
No, I just have two more
points to beat him.

1044
00:43:55,174 --> 00:43:57,552
Monica, that was
also true an hour ago.

1045
00:43:57,594 --> 00:43:59,011
I mean, please,
look at you.

1046
00:43:59,053 --> 00:44:02,181
Your hand is blistered.
You can barely stand.

1047
00:44:02,223 --> 00:44:04,642
Your hair is inexplicable.

1048
00:44:05,810 --> 00:44:08,687
Okay, you've already proven
you're just as good as he is.

1049
